;; namespaces.corpus -- namespace-machinery gap corpus (pending). Every
;; form on this list currently DIVERGES between real Clojure 1.13.0-alpha6
;; and mova; it is a ledger of failures, not aspirational syntax. One
;; session -- a `def`/`intern`/`create-ns` on an earlier line is visible
;; to later lines exactly like a real REPL session.
;;
;; S4 update: `*ns*`/`ns-name`/`the-ns`/`find-ns`/`ns-resolve`/`resolve`/
;; `require` (callable)/`import`/`all-ns` landed and every conforming form
;; that exercised ONLY those was promoted to `tests/conformance/corpus/
;; nsfns.corpus` (see that file's own tail section for exactly which).
;; Still unresolved in mova, exercised below: `create-ns`/`remove-ns`/
;; `intern`/`ns-publics`/`ns-unmap`/`ns-map`/`ns-aliases`/`alias`/
;; `requiring-resolve`/`in-ns`/`use`, plus `resolve`/
;; `ns-resolve` var-PRINTING (mova's core builtins intern BARE --
;; `#'inc` vs real Clojure's `#'clojure.core/inc` -- a separate,
;; unrelated-to-S4 printing-convention gap, not namespace mechanics).
;; `load-string` (W-ADX, wishlist #11) landed and its row was promoted to
;; `tests/conformance/corpus/namespaces.corpus`.
;;
;; NOTE on a genuine curiosity, not a pending case: `(clojure.string/join
;; "," [1 2 3])`-style CALLS (as opposed to the `require`/`alias` step
;; that would normally set them up) sometimes accidentally print the SAME
;; value on both sides. mova resolves any `prefix/name` symbol by
;; stripping everything through the last `/` and looking up the bare
;; `name` in its single global registry, regardless of whether `prefix`
;; was ever `require`d or `alias`ed -- so `str/join`, `set/union`, and an
;; arbitrarily-chosen alias like `cs/intersection` all happen to resolve
;; to mova's global `join`/`union`/`intersection` and return the
;; identical value Clojure's real namespace resolution would. That
;; coincidence was verified and excluded here (it does NOT diverge), but
;; it does not rescue real code: the `require`/`alias` line that real
;; code depends on to set the alias up still fails loudly in mova (see
;; below), and in a real (non-error-tolerant) script that abort happens
;; before the downstream call is ever reached.
(ns-name (create-ns 'foo123))
(intern 'foo123 'bar 42)
(intern 'foo123 'baz 43)
(sort (keys (ns-publics 'foo123)))
(ns-unmap 'foo123 'bar)
(sort (keys (ns-publics 'foo123)))
(ns-resolve 'foo123 'baz)
(do (remove-ns 'foo123) :removed)
(contains? (ns-map 'user) 'inc)
(alias 'cs 'clojure.set)
(requiring-resolve 'clojure.set/union)
